<BaseLayout title="Install FlowCast on Linux with Docker" description="Install the FlowCast Community preview on Linux amd64, review ports and Docker socket risk, then verify your first Icecast broadcast."><section class="page container"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">INSTALLATION</p><h1>Install FlowCast Community</h1><p>The validated preview installer targets an operator-managed Linux amd64 host. Review the installer and security model before running it.</p></header><div class="prose"><h2>Prerequisites</h2><ul><li>Linux amd64, Docker Engine and Docker Compose v2</li><li>2 CPU cores, at least 4 GB RAM and 10 GB free disk plus media</li><li>Free TCP ports <strong>8080</strong> (control/player proxy) and <strong>8010</strong> (direct Icecast)</li></ul><h2>Run the validated tagged installer</h2><pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chourmovs/FlowCast-Community/v0.1.0-rc.7/install.sh | sudo bash -s -- --version 0.1.0-rc.7</code></pre><p>The installer does not install Docker. It verifies the release archive, writes <code>/opt/flowcast</code>, generates a mode-<code>0600</code> <code>.env</code>, pulls versioned service images and waits for health. Existing environment files are not overwritten.</p><aside class="notice"><strong>Root-equivalent Docker access</strong><p>The default validated rc.7 install enables Docker Control. Mounting the Docker socket gives its container root-level control of the host. Never expose the control UI to untrusted users. Pass <code>--no-docker-control</code> to opt out; UI Start/Stop/Restart actions then remain unavailable.</p></aside><h2>Open the interface and broadcast</h2><ol><li>Open <code>http://localhost:8080</code> and use the locally generated credentials.</li><li>Import audio you own or are permitted to use.</li><li>Create or select a playlist and configure its programming.</li><li>Start playout when Docker Control is enabled.</li><li>Listen through <code>/listen/test.mp3</code>, or directly at <code>http://HOST:8010/test.mp3</code>.</li></ol><p>Follow the <a href="https://github.com/chourmovs/FlowCast-Community/blob/main/docs/how-to/first-broadcast.md">complete first-broadcast guide</a>.</p><h2>Diagnose, update and roll back</h2><pre><code>sudo /opt/flowcast/scripts/community/doctor.sh
sudo /opt/flowcast/scripts/community/update.sh --version VERSION</code></pre><p>Back up before changes. The update script supports controlled version changes; use the documented backup/restore path for deliberate rollback. Read <a href="https://github.com/chourmovs/FlowCast-Community/blob/main/docs/community/update-rollback.md">update and rollback</a>, <a href="https://github.com/chourmovs/FlowCast-Community/blob/main/docs/community/backup-restore.md">backup and restore</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/chourmovs/FlowCast-Community/blob/main/docs/community/known-limitations.md">known limitations</a>.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
